.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt PKG-MGR 1
.Os "pkg-mgr 0.1.0 experimental"
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg-mgr
.Nd inspect and manage experimental private-root packages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -root Ar path
.Op Ar options
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a checkout-based host tool for local, staged packages.
Run
.Pa bin/pkg-mgr
from its source checkout.
A standalone installed executable and native Aether package installation are
not implemented.
Root creation and source builds are explicit make operations.
Evidence-bound registration currently requires a root beneath the checkout.
No root privileges are required for the private-root workflows described here.
.Pp
Global options precede the command.
The root must be an absolute path to an existing initialized private directory
owned by the caller with mode 0700.
Paths may contain spaces; control characters in arguments are rejected.
The implementation requires a single writer and a caller-controlled filesystem.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -root Ar path
Select the required private root.
There is no implicit root or environment-based root selection.
.It Fl -format Ar human Ns | Ns Ar tsv
Select human presentation, the default, or unchanged helper output for scripts.
Human results use stdout; status and diagnostics use stderr.
TSV mode preserves ordinary helper streams and exit status.
Wrapper interruption and delivery diagnostics remain text in either mode.
.It Fl -color Ar auto Ns | Ns Ar always Ns | Ns Ar never
Control stderr status colors; the default is auto.
Auto requires a terminal on stderr, TERM other than dumb, and an empty or unset
NO_COLOR variable.
Always overrides NO_COLOR.
Stdout remains uncolored.
.It Fl -plain
Use ASCII human output, escaping control and non-ASCII bytes.
Machine-mode bytes remain unchanged.
No color or animation is used.
.It Fl -quiet
Suppress nonessential start and success status messages.
Results and failures remain visible.
.It Fl -help
Print command help and exit.
This must be the final argument when encountered during option parsing.
.It Fl -version
Print the prototype version and exit.
This must be the final argument when encountered during option parsing.
.El
.Pp
Valued options accept both
.Ql --option=value
and
.Ql --option value .
Repeated identical valued options are accepted; conflicting values are rejected.
Combining color always with plain or TSV mode is a usage error.
There are no progress or verbose options.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
List registered packages.
.It Cm owners
Report package ownership of staged paths.
.It Cm verify
Verify staged regular-file contents and recorded permissions.
No damaged file is repaired.
.It Cm orphans
Report packages outside the dependency closure of requested world roots.
No package is deleted.
.It Cm files Ar name
List recorded files for a package.
.It Cm deps Ar name
List the package's direct dependencies.
.It Cm rdeps Ar name
List its direct reverse dependencies.
.It Cm export Ar name
Create a local binary directory bundle for a registered package.
An occupied destination is rejected.
.It Cm import Ar bundle Ar bundle-sha256 Ar target
Verify and import a local bundle into a fresh private stage.
The bundle path is absolute; its SHA-256 descriptor pin and compiler target
are explicit caller inputs.
This does not establish remote authenticity.
.It Cm recover Ar bundle Ar bundle-sha256 Ar target
Recover a pinned interrupted import only when existing staged content matches
its bundle exactly.
It does not repair or delete mismatched content.
.It Cm preflight Ar bundle Ar bundle-sha256 Ar target
Compare a proposed bundle with current state without replacing it.
Local changes, dependencies and ownership may block replacement.
.It Cm prepare Ar bundle Ar bundle-sha256 Ar target Ar old-record-sha256
Prepare a retained replacement using the exact current package-record pin.
Save the emitted intent digest.
Preparation leaves a pending transaction and does not activate the new package.
An identical proposed record is an unchanged no-op.
.It Cm finish Ar intent-sha256
Revalidate and finish the pending replacement identified by its exact intent pin.
Retain the old payload and records.
Repeated completion is idempotent only while the checked state remains unchanged.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width TMPDIR
.It Ev TMPDIR
Parent directory for private scratch and receipt directories; default is /tmp.
.It Ev TERM
Controls automatic terminal color selection.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
A nonempty value disables automatic color; explicit always overrides it.
.It Ev PATH
Selects host helper programs.
Use a trusted host tool environment; recipes execute trusted maintainer code.
.El
.Sh FILES
Paths below are relative to the selected private root unless noted otherwise.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa .pkg-mgr-root
Initialized fixture marker.
.It Pa state/packages/NAME.tsv
Package records, including file hashes and ordinary permissions.
.It Pa state/world
Editable requested-package roots.
.It Pa stage/NAME
Staged payload, separate from any live system prefix.
.It Pa binaries/NAME
Local binary directory bundle.
.It Pa .replacement
Pending retained-replacement transaction; normal operations remain guarded.
.It Pa replacements/INTENT-SHA256
Completed retained payload and transaction evidence.
.It Pa ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/pkg-mgr-cli.*
Private output buffers, retained if output delivery fails or rendering is interrupted.
They contain out, err and helper-exit when those files were written successfully.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 143
.It 0
Operation succeeded within its declared scope.
.It 1
Helper failure or output-delivery failure.
.It 2
Blocked replacement preflight.
.It 64
Invalid CLI usage.
.It 129, 130, 143
Caught HUP, INT or TERM respectively; completion may be unknown.
.El
.Pp
Other helper statuses pass through during ordinary completion.
Caught signals take precedence over output-delivery failure.
A failing CLI exit can follow a completed mutation.
.Sh RECOVERY
Do not blindly retry a mutation after missing output or an interruption.
The CLI waits for its foreground helper, then attempts to deliver buffered output.
It does not promise cancellation, rollback or termination of helper descendants.
The first caught signal selects the interruption exit status.
SIGKILL and system failure can prevent receipt retention.
.Pp
When output delivery fails, inspect the reported private receipt directory.
Treat raw buffers as untrusted bytes; use a viewer that does not execute terminal
controls.
Recover the emitted intent digest and use the normal pinned finish procedure.
A receipt is an observation, not permission to bypass transaction validation.
Copy needed evidence before temporary-file cleanup.
.Pp
A partial record-publishing copy is preserved and blocks finish retry with
.Ql invalid pending record copy .
A complete pinned copy whose rename failed can be retried.
No automatic repair, pruning or payload deletion is provided.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the source checkout, with sh, GNU Make and a SHA-256 tool available,
create a new private root and build the local text fixture:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
root=$(mktemp -d "$PWD/.pkg-mgr-live-man.XXXXXX")
make -s -f mk/pkg.mk ROOT="$root" init-root
make -s -f mk/pkg.mk ROOT="$root" register
bin/pkg-mgr --root "$root" list
bin/pkg-mgr --root "$root" --plain verify
.Ed
.Pp
The list includes hello-local; verification exits zero and reports verified staged
file contents.
The fixture root remains for inspection; these commands do not write to a live prefix.
For script output, use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bin/pkg-mgr --root "$root" --format tsv \e
    files hello-local
.Ed
.Pp
An unsupported operation is a usage error with status 64:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bin/pkg-mgr --root "$root" remove hello-local
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Pins establish byte identity, not publisher authenticity or freshness.
This prototype does not provide hostile-path race resistance, concurrent-writer
coordination, service activation, live-prefix installation or power-loss durability.
No supported security service or public release approval is implied.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr pkg-state 5
.Pp
The source distribution includes docs/CLI.md for workflow and validation context,
docs/PACKAGE-STATE.md for records, docs/BINARY-PACKAGE.md for bundle formats,
docs/IMPORT-RECOVERY.md for import recovery, and docs/REPLACEMENT-POLICY.md for
replacement details.
